Apple today added a new <a href="https://developer.apple.com/news/?id=fk9ps3gv">subscription retention feature</a> for developers, allowing them to show retention messages when a subscriber goes to cancel.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/11/app-store-subscription-retention.jpg" alt="" width="2048" height="1152" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1075761" /><br/>
Apple says retention messages will appear in the subscription cancellation flow and can include text, images, or a special offer. Retention messages can be added in <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/app-store/">App Store</a> Connect for auto-renewable subscriptions, with options for subscriber eligibility and wait time between messages.<br/>
<br/>
Through a separate Retention Messaging API, developers can choose which messages to show a subscriber based on their subscription details. API access is by request.<br/>
